Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:48:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 23/25] metal: batch all w-planes into one command buffer +
 cache pipelines

gridAccumulate was called once per w-plane, each call recompiling the
MSL source, creating a pipeline, allocating a grid buffer, and paying a
command-buffer wait. Measured per plane: host 0.2ms, gpu 0.5ms, wait
0.9ms - the wait (scheduling, not execution) dominated. New
gridAccumulateBatched encodes all planes into one command buffer and
waits once: 29 planes go from ~46ms to 22ms (gpu 15.4 + wait ~1 +
host bucketing 5.3), bit-identical output (wlayer gate unchanged at
rel_rms 1.28e-05 across w=0..200). Pipeline cache + grid-buffer reuse
also speed the single-call path. Next biggest host cost is bucketing.

